{
  "name": "Start",
  "comment": "Stage 8g (decision 151): the cache stores only the real work's success, never a recovery's result. One cached step\nruns three times (one cache key: the step's place). Try 1 fails and recovers; if that recovery had been cached, try\n2 would be a hit and MaybeFail would not run. Try 2 succeeds and is stored; try 3 is served from the cache. So\n%tries% is 2 only when the recovery is NOT cached AND the cache clause is really bound (dropped: 3).",
